Endpoint What it does <code>GET /v1/models</code> Installed models as OpenAI model objects. <code>GET /v1/models/{id}</code> One model (<code>404</code> + error envelope when unknown). <pre><code>$ curl -s http://127.0.0.1:11440/v1/models
{"object": "list", "data": [{"id": "llama3.2:3b", "object": "model",
 "created": 1789360880, "owned_by": "ollamarun"}, …]}

$ curl -s http://127.0.0.1:11440/v1/models/llama3.2:3b
{"id": "llama3.2:3b", "object": "model", "created": 1789360880,
 "owned_by": "ollamarun"}

$ curl -s http://127.0.0.1:11440/v1/models/nope:latest
{"error": {"message": "model 'nope:latest' not found", "type": "invalid_request_error",
 "param": "model", "code": "model_not_found"}}
</code></pre> <p><code>created</code> is the model's modified time (Unix seconds); <code>owned_by</code> is always <code>ollamarun</code>. The list is fetched from the upstream <code>/api/tags</code>, normalized to tagged names and cached briefly, so a newly pulled model appears without restarting the server.</p> <p>The serve_models allowlist filters this endpoint exactly like every other — a model outside it behaves like an unknown id (<code>404 model_not_found</code>), not a permission error.</p>
